            ],
            "_meanings": [
                "<ab>N.</ab> of a celebrated king and warrior, son of Bṛhadratha.\n [According to a legend, he was born divided in two halves which were put\n together by a Rākṣasī called Jarā, whence the boy was called Jarāsandha.\n He became king of Magadha and Chedi after his fatherʼs death. When he\n heard that Kṛṣṇa had slain his son-in-law Kaṃsa, he gathered a large\n army and besieged Mathurā eighteen times, but was as often repulsed.\n When Yudhiṣṭhira performed the great Rājasūya sacrifice, Kṛṣṇa,\n Arjuna and Bhīma went to the capital of Jarāsandha disguised as Brāhmaṇas,\n chiefly with the object of slaying their enemy and liberating the kings\n imprisoned by him. He, however, refused to release the kings, whereupon\n Bhīma challenged him to a single combat. The challenge was accepted;\n a hard fight ensued, but Jarāsandha was at last overpowered and slain by Bhīma.]\n"
            ]
        },
